    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0360" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to M.
                        Berthemy</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 14, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to our conversation of this
                    morning, I have the honor to communicate to yon a copy of an<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d285-f1"/> opinion rendered by the Hon. Henry Stanbery, the Attorney
                    General, in relation to the right of foreign residents at Valparaiso to
                    reclamations against Chili on account of losses sustained by them in consequence
                    of the bombardment of that city.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Berthemy,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d285-f1" n="*" xml:id="d285-f1-content">
                <p>For this enclosure see instruction to the United States minister to Chili, No.
                    22, of the 2d October, 1866.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
